## Inspection

The six checks announced in my file, as run after the last report.

| Check | Result |
|---|---|
| Each renamed file is a rename in git | Yes. Ten renames, each at 94% likeness or more, except the story at 77%, which also gained the part "In plain words" |
| Each agent stayed in its set | Yes. Every changed file belongs to the set of the agent who reports it |
| No old name left | None outside this discussion, which holds the map and the reports of the rename, and one dated note in the ledger entry |
| Every relative link resolves | 0 broken in 109 documents. Before the job there were 7, all in the issues |
| Each index lists its documents | Yes, for stories, proposals, issues, ledger, memories and discussions |
| Nothing else moved | Lint: 0 errors, and the same warnings as before in both vaults. Derivation: 9 rules, 7 derived, 1 contradiction. Schema check: no violation. Star cover: nothing uncovered. Lean: builds |

No job was sent back. One addition was asked for after the first pass: the
list of discussions in the index, from Carol.

## How the method held

The first discussion was opened after three sessions had already written
into the same files. This one was planned before anyone wrote. A fixed map
of old and new names went out first, each agent got a set of files that no
other agent touched, and links to another agent's documents were corrected
from the map without waiting. No two agents edited one file, and nothing
had to be reconciled afterwards.

## Decisions for the user

1. **Commit.** The change is ready as one commit.
2. **The statuses of a proposal.** Bob's index gives four: `proposed`,
   `accepted`, `rejected`, `superseded`, and says that only the user accepts
   or rejects. The last two and the list of parts are Bob's reading.
3. **Stale prose in the issues and the roadmap.** They still speak of a
   `wiki/` vault in running text. Dave repaired the links and left the prose,
   since rewriting it is not a rename.
4. **Referring to documents by name in link text.** The roadmap still says
   "agents vault issue" where the memory asks for `SLH-I-0001`. Dave asks
   whether link texts everywhere should be changed.
5. **The private memory about cards.** An agent's private memory holds one
   older entry, that cards must carry the arguments of the discussion. By
   the second memory it belongs in `doc/memories/`.
